.TH BIOKIDS\-AI 8 2026\-10\-03 "biokids 0.1.0" "BioKids"
.SH NAME
biokids\-ai \- the BioKids assistant service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B biokids\-ai
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-log\-level
.IR level ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B biokids\-ai
answers the questions a child types or says to the assistant in the
BioKids launcher, with a language model that runs on this computer.
Every question passes a word list and the model's own classification before
it is answered, and every answer passes the word list again; a question that
is refused gets a fixed sentence, and the daemon records it for the parent.
.PP
It runs as the
.B biokids\-ai
system user with no network at all, as the system unit
.BR biokids\-ai.service .
It starts
.BR llama\-server (1)
and, for press\-and\-speak,
.BR whisper\-server (1)
only when a question arrives, and stops them after a few idle minutes.
Its only client is
.BR biokids\-daemon (8),
which decides whether a child may ask at all.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Read the configuration from
.I file
instead of
.IR /etc/biokids/config.toml .
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " level"
One of DEBUG, INFO or WARNING.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/biokids\-ai/ai.sock
The socket the daemon talks to.
.TP
.I /var/lib/biokids\-ai/models
The model files and
.IR selection.json ,
written by
.BR biokids\-ai\-setup (8).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR biokids\-ai\-setup (8),
.BR biokids\-daemon (8)
